From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6358-gauge: Seed again once the battery is
 at rest

The state of charge is seeded once, at probe. On a phone that is the
middle of boot, when the battery typically delivers around an ampere,
so any error in the resistance correction goes into the seed, and the
counter carries it from then on.

Take the seed again the first time the battery current is below
100 mA, where the correction is a few millivolts, unless the seed was
already taken there or the charger has since reported the end of
charge. This is what the recovery state of ab8500_fg does: re-estimate
from the voltage once the current has dropped.

On the Zinwa Q25 the voltage at a light load reads within a few
millivolts of its value at rest, so one sample below the threshold
is enough; after a long heavy load the seed comes out a little low
rather than high.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6358-gauge.c |   13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6358-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6358-gauge.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6358-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6358-gauge.c
@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@
  *
  * The gauge measures the battery current across a shunt and integrates it
  * in a coulomb counter. The state of charge is seeded from the battery's
- * open circuit voltage table, then tracked with the counter and re-anchored
- * at 100% whenever the charger reports the end of charge.
+ * open circuit voltage table, taken again once the battery is at rest if the
+ * first seed was taken under load, then tracked with the counter and
+ * re-anchored at 100% whenever the charger reports the end of charge.
  */
 
 #include <linux/bits.h>
@@ -45,6 +46,7 @@
 #define MT6358_FG_OCV_SAMPLES		4
 #define MT6358_FG_OCV_CELSIUS		25
 #define MT6358_FG_IDLE_UA		50000
+#define MT6358_FG_RELAX_UA		100000
 #define MT6358_FG_POLL_MS		(10 * MSEC_PER_SEC)
 
 struct mt6358_gauge {
@@ -58,6 +60,7 @@
 	struct mutex lock;
 	u32 shunt_uohm;
 	bool anchored;
+	bool relaxed;
 	s32 anchor_count;
 	int anchor_uah;
 	int capacity;
@@ -196,6 +199,7 @@
 	gauge->anchor_uah = mult_frac(gauge->info->charge_full_design_uah,
 				      soc, 100);
 	gauge->anchored = true;
+	gauge->relaxed = abs(current_ua) < MT6358_FG_RELAX_UA;
 
 	dev_dbg(gauge->dev, "OCV %lld uV at %lld uA: %d%%\n", ocv, current_ua,
 		soc);
@@ -234,7 +238,10 @@
 			gauge->anchor_count = sample.count;
 			gauge->anchor_uah = gauge->info->charge_full_design_uah;
 			gauge->anchored = true;
-		} else if (!gauge->anchored) {
+			gauge->relaxed = true;
+		} else if (!gauge->anchored ||
+			   (!gauge->relaxed &&
+			    abs(sample.current_ua) < MT6358_FG_RELAX_UA)) {
 			ret = mt6358_gauge_seed(gauge);
 			if (ret)
 				break;
-- 
